  "tax_note": "Adult-use cannabis is subject to a 12% sales and use tax, up from 9% on July 1, 2025 (Comptroller of Maryland).",
  "summary": "Maryland converted its medical dispensaries to adult-use sales on July 1, 2023, and the market has grown every year since. Dispensaries sold $101.5 million in September 2026, including $84.6 million to adult-use consumers. Total sales were $1.14 billion in 2024 and $1.17 billion in 2025, and January-September 2026 sales are about 5% ahead of the same period of 2025. Adult-use growth has more than offset a steady fall in medical sales. Maryland draws shoppers from Washington, D.C., Virginia and Delaware, where legal store access is limited or prices are higher.",
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much cannabis does Maryland sell a month?",
      "a": "Maryland dispensaries sold $101.5 million in September 2026: $84.6 million adult-use and $16.9 million medical, according to the Maryland Cannabis Administration."
    },
    {
      "q": "How much cannabis did Maryland sell in 2025?",
      "a": "About $1.17 billion, of which $918.1 million was adult-use, based on MCA monthly data."
    },
    {
      "q": "What is the cannabis tax in Maryland?",
      "a": "Adult-use purchases carry a 12% sales and use tax, raised from 9% on July 1, 2025. Medical patients do not pay it."
    }
  ],
